From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] skw: refuse recovery without a boot device

A chip exception schedules skw_recovery_mode(), which reloads the chip
through the boot device. When that device failed to probe, boot_data is
NULL and the first exception oopses on it, and an oops panics the box.
Refuse recovery then: the radio stays down, the box stays up.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/seekwaveplatform_lite/sdio/skw_sdio_main.c b/drivers/seekwaveplatform_lite/sdio/skw_sdio_main.c
index e6ace19..1e524f3 100644
--- a/drivers/seekwaveplatform_lite/sdio/skw_sdio_main.c
+++ b/drivers/seekwaveplatform_lite/sdio/skw_sdio_main.c
@@ -2083,6 +2083,12 @@ int skw_recovery_mode(void)
 {
 	int ret=0;
 	struct skw_sdio_data_t *skw_sdio = skw_sdio_get_data();
+
+	/* the boot device reloads the chip: without it, refuse rather than oops the box */
+	if (!skw_sdio || !skw_sdio->boot_data) {
+		skw_sdio_err("no boot device: the chip cannot be recovered\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
 	skw_sdio_info("the CHIPID:%s \n", (char *)&skw_sdio->chip_id);
 	ret = skw_sdio_recovery_debug_status();
 #ifdef CONFIG_SKW_FREE_FIRMWARE_MEM_SUPPORT
